      "problem": "Which of the following plots is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n- The domain is all real numbers except at the integer multiples of $\\pi $: $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…$\n\n- The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The period of the function is $\\pi .$\n\n- There is no minimum or maximum value.\n\n- The zeros occur at $x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…$\n\n- The graph has vertical asymptotes at the points that are not in the domain: $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ and at each asymptote, the graph tends to $-\\infty $ from the left and $\\infty $ from the right.\n\nOf the given plots, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254348/assets/1d0510d5dc22d3ecb81f4cbaa67789c84b1fdc1a40065c0d2527683271e261a6.png)",
